<%# crosswire:contract v1 %>
<%#
  Deliberately dumb — every attribute decision lives in Crosswire::UI::ToastViewport,
  so this file is safe to restyle, shadow, or eject. See docs/DECISIONS.md D6.

  Render this ONCE per politeness level, in the layout, BEFORE any toast exists — "the
  aria-live rule from the corpus", see the presenter's own docstring. `content` is
  populated only by the server-rendered-flash-toasts rendering path
  (`cw.toast_viewport { ... }`); the Turbo-Stream-appended path targets this same
  element's `id` later and needs no block here at all — an empty container on first
  paint is the normal, expected case, not a gap.

  Locals:
    viewport  Crosswire::UI::ToastViewport
    content   String or nil — already-captured block content (zero or more `cw.toast`
              calls)
%>
<div <%= cw_attrs(viewport.root_attrs) %>><%= content %></div>
